### Author response to Round 4

Nine of twelve checks now ACCEPT (1,2,3,5,7,9,10,11,12). Three blocking issues
remained plus two new boundary contradictions. All addressed:

- **CHECK 4 → "guaranteed termination" removed.** I4 now says process-group
  ownership provides **best-effort** termination and explicitly names the defeat
  mechanisms (`setsid()`, `process_group()`, Job-Object breakaway). It also notes
  that WebCodex's own `remote_shell`/`ssh`/`detached_job` Unix paths already
  spawn outside `ManagedChild`, making this a live property of the current code
  rather than a hypothetical.
- **CHECK 6 → PE-06c precision added.** The claim is narrowed: uid separation
  denies the **mode-protected** case (the security-relevant one, e.g. `0600`
  credential files), because access to the *inode* is denied. A world-readable
  outside inode remains readable through the link — but it was already readable
  by its original path, so there is **no incremental exposure**. The guarantee is
  restated as "no additional access beyond what the identity already had", which
  is the property that actually holds. It is also noted that macOS has no
  `fs.protected_hardlinks` equivalent, so uid separation is the only mechanism
  covering PE-06a'.
- **CHECK 8 → plugin-disable gate added to P0.** P0 acceptance criterion (6) now
  requires a plugin/hook disable gate with plugins **disabled by default** until
  P8 defines the contract, and P0's rollback explicitly forbids reverting that
  gate. P8's rollback is corrected: rolling back P8 must leave hooks **disabled**,
  not "restore current behaviour", because current behaviour is the undefined
  path I17 says must not run.
- **New defect 1 → secret boundary made explicit.** The NET-11 note no longer
  relies on a circular "credentials are denied". It now defines **two disjoint
  sets** with their own deny rules — secret patterns **inside** the project tree
  and well-known credential locations **outside** it — and states plainly that a
  profile granting "read the project root" does **not** satisfy the row. The
  incompleteness of the pattern list is stated as a documented limitation, and
  `I16` remains `PARTIAL`. P1b acceptance criteria (9) and (10) were added.
- **New defect 2 → control-plane reachability downgraded.** `§4` and
  `OSS_RESEARCH_EVIDENCE.md §2.5` no longer assert "not model-reachable". They
  state that reachability is the **intent**, that `src/tool_runtime/helpers.rs:146`
  was classified model-reachable, that the call graph is unproven, and that no
  document may make the categorical claim until the P0 inventory and CP-04 test
  establish it.

