ROUND 11 — FIXES APPLIED
================================================================================

The reviewer's central finding is accepted in full and is treated as the organizing
principle of this round: **dispatch policy is a per-call, not per-action, boundary.**
The author had already discovered this for the network and external-read cases
(item 9e) but had then written the *same* class of over-claim in the opposite
direction — `DENY` where nothing was enforced. The round-11 repair is therefore
structural rather than local: it introduces a value that makes the honest answer
expressible.

FIX 1 (newly raised — matrix §4 `proc.signal.external` / `agent.spawn.<id>`).
  `COMPONENT_REUSE_MATRIX.md §4` now opens with a four-valued outcome vocabulary:

      ALLOW          — a mechanism permits the effect, and the mechanism is named.
      ASK            — a mechanism can interpose and interposes; the interposing
                       component is named in the cell or the note below it.
      DENY           — a mechanism refuses the effect, unconditionally on this surface.
      NOT_ENFORCED   — no mechanism observes this effect on this surface. This is a
                       statement about coverage, not a permission.

  `NOT_ENFORCED` is explicitly *not* read as "safe" and explicitly *not* read as
  "refused". The two rows change from `ASK`/in-shell-`DENY` to
  `ASK` (mediated) / `NOT_ENFORCED` (in-child).

FIX 2 (newly raised — P5 criterion 4). Destructive operations and unknown binaries are
  now `NOT_ENFORCED` when performed inside a shell or build process in `AUTO`, and the
  criterion says so in the same sentence that promises mediation for the same classes
  in the mediated path. The scope limit is stated rather than left to be discovered.

FIX 3 (CHECK 5 — P1c criterion 7). The single loopback fixture could only ever prove a
  localhost rule; it could not prove the arbitrary-destination property the criterion
  is about. The criterion now names **two** positive fixtures: a loopback listener for
  the localhost rule, and a *reachable* non-loopback destination for the
  arbitrary-destination rule. `203.0.113.10` is retained in the text but marked as the
  unreachable literal that motivated the correction, not as the test target.

FIX 4 (CHECK 5 — P1c criterion 8, `PROXY_SPAWN_BINDING`). "Per-spawn" was asserted over
  a mechanism that is a transferable bearer. The plan now distinguishes a
  kernel-tied capability from a bearer capability, and states that a bearer capability
  remains `NOT_ENFORCED` for per-spawn attribution until a transferability test passes.
  The gate condition is no longer "the grant is per-spawn" but "the grant is
  attributable to one child and cannot be moved to another".

FIX 5 (CHECK 6 — PE-06b / PE-06c). "Strict on all surfaces" contradicted the TOCTOU
  residual stated two paragraphs later. The two vectors are now split by **admission
  stage** instead of by surface: pre-admission (the walk has not yet completed, the
  tool call has not been dispatched) is `DENY`; post-admission (inside a running
  shell, where a link created after the walk is not re-walked) is `NOT_ENFORCED`.
  The summary row was updated to match rather than to keep the stronger claim.

FIX 6 (CHECK 8 — P8 dependency). P8's criterion 5 requires re-evaluating hook-mutated
  arguments under the P2 policy engine. The dependency graph read `P1b ──▶ P8`, which
  permits hooks to be enabled before that engine exists. The graph is now
  `P1b ──▶ P2 ──▶ P8`, and P8 carries an explicit `DEPENDENCY` row naming both P1b and
  P2 so the constraint is visible at the phase itself, not only in the graph.

CONSISTENCY SWEEP RUN MECHANICALLY AFTER THE FIXES (not by eye):
  - LOC table re-measured: 19 rows summing to **4,750 / 8,300**, matching the printed
    total. Round 11 added no phase.
  - `OSS_RESEARCH_EVIDENCE.md §8` numbering re-verified as continuous
    (`1 … 9, 9a–9f, 10, 11`).
  - Retired-term sweep: `UNSANDBOXED_BACKEND` survives only in the three places that
    explicitly record its withdrawal (matrix/implementation plan/evidence) and
