FIX 1 (CHECK 4 + a new defect — the category error, and it was mine).
  The round-17 residual gate denied *non-catalogued executable paths*. Round 18
  withdrew it. An uncatalogued **spawn site** can launch a binary that **is** in
  the closure — `/bin/sh` is the obvious case — so denying *other* executables
  does nothing about it. Unknown **reachability** and executable **identity** are
  different properties, and only the first is what CP-04 leaves open. The gate is
  now at the **spawn API**: criterion (1b) makes the refusal **unconditional**,
  so it binds catalogued and uncatalogued callers alike, and (1c) keeps the
  reporting obligation. Stated once, in the plan: *this closes the risk, not the
  uncertainty* — whether any uncatalogued model-reachable site exists is still
  `UNKNOWN`. A residual that is reported but still reachable is not a disclosed
  limit; it is an unclosed gate.
FIX 2 (CHECK 11) — CP-02 restated as **attachment for the catalogued set plus
  unconditional refusal for the rest**, which is checkable, instead of complete
  attachment, which is not available. CP-02 and CP-01 no longer disagree.
FIX 3 (CHECK 5 + a new defect) — P1c criterion 6's literal-IP/localhost release
