--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
LESSON LEDGER — what round 18 added to the failure taxonomy
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
L1. **A demotion must propagate to every place the property is asserted.** I6
    was demoted in round 17 and the same claim re-asserted in §13 and PI-01 in
    round 18. Position, not just wording, is what has to be audited.
L2. **A repair added *beside* a claim does not amend it.** Round 18 added
    P1a (1a)/(1b)/(1c) while criterion (1) kept the universal wording, leaving
    two incompatible requirements in one cell.
L3. **Enumerate the set, or admit it is not enumerable — and then say which.**
    "Every model-reachable spawn" is unactionable; the honest forms are a
    bounded catalogue plus `UNKNOWN`, or a **mechanism-level** refusal that does
    not depend on the set at all. The second is what closed CHECK 4.
L4. **A per-process boundary is not a per-surface boundary.** A sandbox profile
    constrains processes; it says nothing about synthetic input events, so any
    claim of the form "the model cannot reach X" must name the route, not the
    asset.
L5. **Vector preconditions must be mutually consistent.** NET-06b asserted a
    property about an execution site that its own precondition removed. When a
    row's outcome depends on a lifetime, the lifetime belongs in the row.
L6. **Conditional mechanisms are conjunctions, not adjectives.** "Independent of
    the kernel's rule" is a conjunction written as an adverb.

