    five-cell finding — strong claim first, correction appended — is an
    overclaim, not a missing deliverable. **The accurate statement is that this
    review has two distinct failure modes — a claim stronger than its
    evidence, and a promise never delivered — and **this review does not
    rank them, because the history contains no count of either and L60
    forbids manufacturing one.** The second is cheaper to *fix* in a given
    instance, since its fix is a verification step rather than an argument. Fix:
    before running a review, verify that every noun the prompt calls a deliverable
    is actually concatenated into the prompt, print its size, and publish a hash.** Three separate instances (P1b(12), EX-13/EX-14, the round-27 log)
    were each introduced while fixing an earlier round's "missing gate" finding.
    After each, the document set grew a new promised artifact with no producer
    and no submission. **Fix: before running a review, verify that every noun the
    prompt calls a deliverable is actually concatenated into the prompt, and
    print its size.**
L49. **A fix that widens a list can introduce a circularity.** Round 27 added
    (4)/(9)/(10) to the proxy-path gate and typed criterion (6) — the gate's own
    opening rule — into it. Widening a set is an edit like any other and needs
