Blocking count over the last three rounds: 9 -> 6 -> 5.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
THE DECISIVE FINDING: ROUND 31'S FIX CREATED A SELF-CONTRADICTION
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Round 31's fixes were structurally correct -- each superseded claim was replaced
at its own position rather than annotated behind. The reviewer accepted that
structure and blocked on something the fix created.

P3 (7b') opened with "the approval affordance is rendered only into a surface no
model-driven route can reach" and then conceded, one paragraph later, that the
process-route confirmation UI's reachability from synthetic input is UNMEASURED.
Round 31's newly-raised finding is exact and is the whole of this round:

  "P3(7b') simultaneously asserts that its displayed approval UI is unreachable
   and says its reachability from synthetic input is unmeasured. These are
   incompatible descriptions of the SAME process-route UI, not merely different
   UI routes."

**That is not a wording defect. It is two claims about one object, and no
editorial operation separates them.** Round 31 tried to fix a wording problem with
a wording operation, which is why it produced a new one.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
THE DECISION: STOP DELIVERING APPROVAL (L71)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
The property in question -- that a displayed confirmation cannot be operated by a
UI-automation route -- has no producer in this plan (P3-R, `NOT_ENFORCED`). There
are exactly two honest resolutions: produce the mechanism, or do not ship the
feature. Round 32 takes the second.

  **P3 no longer delivers approval. It delivers the machinery and renders no
  affordance at all.** The phase heading is now "P3 -- Local control channel +
  approval machinery (renders no model-reachable approval affordance; `ASK`
  resolves to `DENY` in this phase)". Criterion (7b') reads "No approval
  affordance is rendered for the model to reach, by any route, in this phase ...
  the local confirmation dialog is not displayed at all, and every `ASK` resolves
  to `DENY`". The goal says the same thing first, and states that **nothing in P3
  may be described as human approval.**

This is the conservative direction and it is the one the review has been pointing
at since round 29: "Withholding the feature is the right safety posture, but not a
completed approval phase." Four consequences were propagated, because leaving any
of them would recreate the contradiction elsewhere:

  - P5 criterion (5): `APPROVE_FOR_ME` routes ASK to the reviewer and unresolved
    cases to **`DENY`**. A reviewer `ESCALATE` is a terminal `DENY`, not a
    hand-off to a person -- the reviewer in that mode is a model, so escalating to
    a human was always the only honest ceiling and it is now explicit.
  - P5 `ROLLBACK`: falls back to `AUTO` with **no approval surface at all**.
  - `SECURITY_TEST_VECTORS.md` AR-03: reviewer `ESCALATE` -> **`DENY`**, "there is
    no human-approval surface to fall through to, because P3 renders none".
  - `REFERENCE_ARCHITECTURE.md` §2 flow: `ESCALATE` -> **DENY**, with the note
    that §7 describes the machinery, which exists, and the affordance, which this
    plan withholds.

Nothing was weakened to achieve this. Every path that previously reached a human
decision now reaches `DENY`, which is the direction the floors already pointed.

